%% aoneahsan-cccs-postgres-multitenancy-rbac — full flow
flowchart TD
    trigger([Access-control work]) --> what{What are you doing?}

    what -->|designing the tenant model| where{Where does membership live?}
    where -->|JWT claim| stale[NO. A claim is stamped at login.<br/>Revocation waits for the next refresh]
    where -->|membership table| good[tenant_members user_id, tenant_id, role<br/>Read at query time. Revoke = DELETE]
    stale --> good
    good --> roles[Two levels, never conflated:<br/>platform_role on the user<br/>tenant role on the MEMBERSHIP]
    roles --> onewriter[/One writer. A synced copy on the<br/>user row gives two answers<br/>to one question/]

    what -->|adding a role or permission| perm{Storing a permission<br/>list per user?}
    perm -->|yes| no2[NO. It sits on a row the user can write,<br/>drifts from the roles, and nobody<br/>can answer 'who can do X']
    perm -->|no| registry[Role to capability REGISTRY in code.<br/>User carries a role; server derives]
    no2 --> registry
    registry --> enforce[/Server enforces, client explains.<br/>A hidden button stops nothing/]

    what -->|writing a policy| deny[Deny by default.<br/>Explicit policy per table.<br/>NO catch-all]
    deny --> prove[🔴 Provable from the query's OWN filters]
    prove --> ex[Policy reads tenant_id<br/>=> EVERY list, count and aggregate<br/>must filter on tenant_id]
    ex --> why[/A list fails when ANY candidate<br/>row fails the policy. Being inside<br/>a tenant is invisible to the planner/]

    what -->|a list 403s but a single read works| diag[That IS this rule.<br/>Add the filter the policy reads]

    what -->|verifying| who{Which account<br/>are you testing as?}
    who -->|admin| trap[🔴 STOP. The admin branch passes<br/>silently. A sibling project reported<br/>PASS twice on a feature that was<br/>100% broken for real users]
    who -->|least-privileged role| probe[Three-way probe]
    trap --> probe
    probe --> p1[1. member -> 200 WITH ROWS]
    p1 --> p2[2. non-member -> 403]
    p2 --> p3[3. member, filter REMOVED -> 403<br/>proves the policy, not the filter]
    p3 --> seed{Did any probe<br/>return 200 with 0 rows?}
    seed -->|yes| vacuous[Proves NOTHING — zero rows<br/>satisfies any policy.<br/>Seed data, probe again]
    seed -->|no| pass([Verified])
